+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Merge Patch and returns the
+merged document as a new value; neither input is mutated. Object patches merge recursively, `null` removes
+a member, and any non-object patch (including arrays) replaces the target. A `null` inside a patch that
+replaces a non-object target is dropped, as the RFC's algorithm specifies. `__proto__` is treated as an
+ordinary member and never reaches a prototype.
+
+```ts
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: 1 }, { a: null, d: 2 }); // { c: 1, d: 2 }
+```
